    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0225" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4/190½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State of a Conversation
                        with the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geddes</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">September 20, 1921</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1921-09-20">September 20,
                        1921</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract<anchor n="89" xml:id="d110-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <p>The Ambassador said that he had been instructed by his Government to say that
                    they were satisfied with the proposed agenda<anchor n="90" xml:id="d110-f2"/>
                    save that they desired to add the subject of the Panama Canal tolls.</p>
                <pb facs="0226" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>
                <p>The Secretary said that he did not think it advisable that this subject should be
                    brought into the Conference; that in his opinion it was a matter to be dealt
                    with diplomatically between the Governments of Great Britain and the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador said that it was the view of his Government that it was a question
                    not alone between Great Britain and the United States but affecting other
                    governments and so would appropriately be brought into the Conference.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
